"Introducing GPT-5.3-Codex—the most powerful, interactive, and productive Codex yet - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/introducing-gpt-5-3-codex-the-most-powerful-interactive-and-productive-codex-yet/1373453)\nciteturn31560search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; kanzariyamihir February 6, 2026, 7:06am 7 ... aguirrerjg February 7, 2026, 12:43am 12\n  * Broader Professional Workflows: Enhanced productivity in tasks like documentation, presentations, data analysis, and structured outputs\n  * Optimized Efficiency: Higher accuracy - fewer tokens\n\nGPT-5.3-Codex is available today for all paid ChatGPT users via the Codex app, CLI, IDE extensions, and web. API access is rolling out soon.\n\nTry GPT-5.3-Codex now and let us know what you build!\n\naf0r February 5, 2026, 6:41pm 2\n\nFeels like being a kid, and getting gta 4 for the xbox 360, damn what a time to be alive, thanks to the openAI team they are incredible.\n\nandrea.panizza75 February 5, 2026, 8:59pm 4\n\nThis February feels like Christmas! Image: :santa_claus:\n\nsam.saffron February 5, 2026, 10:04pm 5\n\nAfter playing with this for an hour, it is pretty fantastic.\n\nMy favorite thing about the new model besides speed is the way it is fine tuned to do “red green” development.\n\nIt almost insists to write failing tests prior to building features. Great move by Open AI\n\nmatt98 February 5, 2026, 11:37pm 6\n\nI’m loving the coding, but not the speed. I don’t know if it’s a load issue, but it’s probably 3x slower than 5.2 codex in my experience so far today. Painfully slow. I’m hoping this is just a launch day issue.\n\nkanzariyamihir February 6, 2026, 7:06am 7\n\nAre there any pricing changes compared to the 5.2 codex?\n\nmerefield February 6, 2026, 8:36am 8\n\nAs @VeitB stated, API access has not yet been released so I assume prices are TBD too.. Auth via ChatGPT for the time being and the price you pay is your monthly sub.\n\nmerefield February 6, 2026, 2:45pm 9\n\nImage VeitB:\n\n> Try GPT-5.3-Codex now and let us know what you build!\n\nI’ve been building this, which I think is quite appropriate, all things considered.\n\ngithub.com\n\nImage\n\n### GitHub - merefield/termcourse: A terminal based client to access Discourse...\n\nA terminal based client to access Discourse instances, supporting API keys, username/password (and with MFA token)\n\n(FYI works on many Discourse instances, but not yet on this site as this site blocks automated remote username password interaction Image: :frowning: - the malicious bots always spoil the fun )\n\n(And 5.3 is definitely proving to be faster! Image: :racing_car: )\n\n_j February 6, 2026, 10:03pm 11\n\nNo luck getting the VSCode latest “release” or “preview” extension logged in via the “Sign in with ChatGPT” flow. It launches a browser, wanting your login, password, (then one-factor on a mobile device that doesn’t even support ChatGPT app any more, then needing “try with email”) by email login code, then simply fails. Tried having it launch OS default browser Firefox, Chromium, and Edge - all fail.\n\nimage785×120 2.65 KB\n\nAnd where’s the “store”: false option?\n\naguirrerjg February 7, 2026, 12:43am 12\n\nHi everyone,\n\nI’m a ChatGPT Plus subscriber, but I can’t seem to find the GPT-5.3-Codex model in my model picker/dropdown menu.\n\nIs this model currently being rolled out gradually, or should it be available to all Plus users immediately? I’ve tried refreshing and logging out/in, but it still doesn’t appear.\n\nAny advice would be appreciated. Thanks!\n\nCaptura de pantalla 2026-02-06 a la(s) 7.39.12 p.m.1174×1572 68.8 KB\n\nMb February 7, 2026, 1:52am 13\n\nBased on my testing so far, yes, it is faster, but I would argue that it is neither better nor smarter than version 5.2 yet. I’m getting mixed results. In some areas, the approach is better, but not necessarily much better, while in others, it goes down some fairly strange routes. One of these general issues is trying to solve bugs with fallbacks instead of fixing the issue itself (i.e. migrating around it). But let’s wait and see; it’s still early days. In any case, the advancements in the last 6 months have been amazing. Just as info.\n\nPaulBellow February 7, 2026, 2:17am 14\n\nImage Mb:\n\n> In any case, the advancements in the last 6 months have been amazing. Just as info.\n\nI think a lot of people forget how fast the industry is moving when you really think about it. ChatGPT had a lot of users super quick. The scaling of things now is crazy. I think we’ll begin to see the models improving themselves soon … then maybe another hockey-stick moment? I believe so, but we shall see.\n\nYeah, though, we’ve become so accustomed to new, better, faster, cheaper, I think we sometimes forget how fast everything is moving. There’s not enough electricity to really keep brute-forcing it yet, so I’m wondering if there will be other breakthroughs that will accelerate it even more.\n\nInteresting thread. Thanks to everyone participating!\n\nmerefield February 7, 2026, 4:46am 15\n\nI had a similar problem In `codex-cli`, I had to update the version and enter `/model` then it appeared.\n\nTry logging out and logging back in?\n\nLasse_Larsen February 7, 2026, 12:19pm 16\n\nI have a plus account why am I getting this error\n\n{“detail”:“The ‘gpt-5.3-codex’ model is not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account.”}\n\n_j February 7, 2026, 1:38pm 17\n\nImage Lasse_Larsen:\n\n> I have a plus account why am I getting this error\n\nI cannot answer - I have a free account, installed a brand new VSCode on a new computer image with the offered extension for Codex - by OpenAI, logged in via ChatGPT. Contrary to first message cut-and-paste “available today in all Codex surfaces”, but in agreement with its “available today for all paid ChatGPT users”, it is not available in this surface pre-populated into the models listing.\n\nimage425×380 8.27 KB\n\nBy config.toml “model” and profile I get the same erroneous error message text with a falsehood:\n\nimage395×202 4.32 KB\n\nmerefield February 7, 2026, 2:36pm 18\n\nI’ve found an issue that’s occuring too regularly to ignore.\n\nOften I find the bot saying it will do something and then simply stops and I have to push it to carry on, e.g.Image: :sweat_smile:\n\n> › lower the top threshold a bit more\n\nI’ll lower the stats breakpoint further (a bit below 150) and keep the rest unchanged. I’ll patch and syntax-check\n\n----tumble weed----\n\n> › do it\n\nAnd then it starts doing it.\n\nThat’s happened twice in the last 10 mins!\n\nyaovisamah February 10, 2026, 7:28am 20\n\nImage: :grin: Oh yeah, it so awesome!, they are doing so well, great team behind the openAI projects\n\nKillBill February 10, 2026, 10:42pm 22\n\nImage Mb:\n\n> One of these general issues is trying to solve bugs with fallbacks instead of fixing the issue itself (i.e. migrating around it).\n\n“One of these general issues is trying to solve bugs with fallbacks instead of fixing the issue itself (i.e. migrating around it).”\n\nI hate to see it happening in any version of GPT.\nIt always abuses guard-checks, fallbacks, null-checks where it’s not needed at all.\n\nIt’s often applies dirty changes to the clean code base, but it’s not related exactly to the codex 5.3 as I said it was happening forever.\n\nIt cannot create the code-base native changes if you don’t not control it directly step-by-step.\n\nANC February 12, 2026, 5:00am 23\n\nSo cool I like it . I will try now--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUndoing code changes is not possible on a per-file basis - #3 by Throstur - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/undoing-code-changes-is-not-possible-on-a-per-file-basis/1373553/3)\nciteturn31560search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; Throstur February 7, 2026, 12:27am 3\n\n# Undoing code changes is not possible on a per-file basis\n\nCodex\n\nbug, feature-request\n\nThrostur February 7, 2026, 12:27am 3\n\nThank you @_j for your helpful feedback on my issue. The use case popped up when I had asked Codex in the code extension ( `code` package from arch repos) to do some stuff that was vaguely related. It ended up changing two files which happened to be completely independent from each other aside from the fact that one of them was a javascript that needs to work to load the other file.\n\nWell the changes borked the javascript, but I still wanted to test the changes to the other file. I had to choose: discard everything, spend tokens on communicating with LLM (even though I was done with the session and didn’t care about the LLM’s future context) or painstakingly editing one of the two files by hand.\n\nLike most good engineers I’m lazy by nature and always want to find the easiest/best way to do things long-term. This time it means spending a bunch of time documenting the problem for my future self (carrying the can), but at the time I just told the LLM exactly what I wanted to do instead (I kicked the can, spending tokens for “nothing”) because I couldn’t gauge how accurate the changes I did want to test were. Not that the end result matters, but I ended up discarding all of the changes anyway… but I could have been discarding something useful, if I hadn’t checked first!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow to allow Codex connection to Docker in local environment? - #2 by EricGT - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/how-to-allow-codex-connection-to-docker-in-local-environment/1373567/2)\nciteturn31560search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; EricGT February 7, 2026, 1:18pm 2\n\nEricGT February 7, 2026, 1:18pm 2\n\nIf you have not, consider searching the GitHub OpenAI Codex issues, both open and closed\n\nImage GitHub\n\nImage\n\n### openai/codex\n\nLightweight coding agent that runs in your terminal - openai/codex\n\nand also the GitHub OpenAI Codex discussions\n\nImage GitHub\n\nImage\n\n### openai codex · Discussions\n\nExplore the GitHub Discussions forum for openai codex. Discuss code, ask questions & collaborate with the developer community.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMore detailed information about models - #3 by redsmurph - Feedback - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/more-detailed-information-about-models/1373598/3)\nciteturn31560search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; redsmurph February 7, 2026, 9:59pm 3\n\n# More detailed information about models\n\nAPI Feedback\n\nredsmurph February 7, 2026, 9:59pm 3\n\n“In terms of “friendly names”, you can employ only “aliases” without dates”\n\nThat’s not a friendly name. The friendly (as in user-facing) name for e.g. “gpt-5-mini” would be “GPT-5 mini” as per OpenAI specification. Relying on “magic” would be fraught with errors considering the varying naming syntax of OpenAI models.\n\n“Here’s hours of labor compiling and verifying where OpenAI documentation is lacking, that you get for free today in consumable format”\n\nThanks.\n\nMy suggestion was mainly directed at OpenAI, alternatively to get hints about moderated repositories listing models and features.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUndoing code changes is not possible on a per-file basis - #4 by Throstur - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/undoing-code-changes-is-not-possible-on-a-per-file-basis/1373553/4)\nciteturn31560search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; Throstur February 7, 2026, 12:30am 4\n\n# Undoing code changes is not possible on a per-file basis\n\nCodex\n\nbug, feature-request\n\nThrostur February 7, 2026, 12:30am 4\n\nimage448×238 9.63 KB\n\nFor reference, I attach a screenshot of a two-file edit in the extension and the right-click context, which could do with a “selectively undo only this patch” option.\n\nSure, if it’s dangerous hold my hand a bit and give me a warning… but don’t glue my hand to yours and prevent me from letting go. (Ironic that giving agency here actually means sacrificing a lot of individual abilities that you wouldn’t normally when delegating)\n\nI also noticed that “Request changes” doesn’t seem to do anything, but since I didn’t test it thoroughly it is not a part of this “issue”.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhen changing thread in Codex app chat is rendered from the beginning.: need to manually scroll to the end of the chat - Codex CLI - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/when-changing-thread-in-codex-app-chat-is-rendered-from-the-beginning-need-to-manually-scroll-to-the-end-of-the-chat/1373595)\nciteturn31560search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; SamiGoesAI February 7, 2026, 5:58pm 1\n\n# When changing thread in Codex app chat is rendered from the beginning.: need to manually scroll to the end of the chat\n\nCodex Codex CLI\n\napp\n\nSamiGoesAI February 7, 2026, 5:58pm 1\n\nHello there. Anyone solve this really annoying “feature” that when you are changing from one thread to another, discussion is rendered from the beginning and you need to scroll all the way down to get to the latest conversations.\n\nEricGT February 7, 2026, 6:36pm 2\n\nTwo ideas\n\n  1. Use codex /feedback\n\nCommand: `/feedback`\nPurpose: Send logs to the Codex maintainers.\nWhen to use it: Report issues or share diagnostics with support.\n\nImage developers.openai.com\n\nImage\n\n### Slash commands in Codex CLI\n\nControl Codex during interactive sessions\n\n  2. Search and possibly submit a Codex issue\n\n`https://github.com/openai/codex/issues`\n\nImage GitHub\n\nImage\n\n### openai/codex\n\nLightweight coding agent that runs in your terminal - openai/codex--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing GPT-5.3-Codex—the most powerful, interactive, and productive Codex yet - #12 by aguirrerjg - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/introducing-gpt-5-3-codex-the-most-powerful-interactive-and-productive-codex-yet/1373453/12)\nciteturn31560search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 7 months ago; aguirrerjg February 7, 2026, 12:43am 12\n\n# Introducing GPT-5.3-Codex—the most powerful, interactive, and productive Codex yet\n\nannouncement, codex\n\naguirrerjg February 7, 2026, 12:43am 12\n\nHi everyone,\n\nI’m a ChatGPT Plus subscriber, but I can’t seem to find the GPT-5.3-Codex model in my model picker/dropdown menu.\n\nIs this model currently being rolled out gradually, or should it be available to all Plus users immediately? I’ve tried refreshing and logging out/in, but it still doesn’t appear.\n\nAny advice would be appreciated. Thanks!\n\nCaptura de pantalla 2026-02-06 a la(s) 7.39.12 p.m.1174×1572 68.8 KB--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nResponses API: empty output_text (no message item) when status=incomplete due to max_output_tokens (reasoning-only output) - API - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/responses-api-empty-output-text-no-message-item-when-status-incomplete-due-to-max-output-tokens-reasoning-only-output/1373609)\nciteturn31560search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; TheodorNEngoy February 7, 2026, 11:09pm 1 ... _j February 7, 2026, 11:15pm 2\n\n# Responses API: empty output_text (no message item) when status=incomplete due to max_output_tokens (reasoning-only output)\n\nAPI\n\ncodex, reasoning, responses-api\n\nTheodorNEngoy February 7, 2026, 11:09pm 1\n\n# Draft: Developer Forum Post (Blank `message` Output Under Tight Budgets)\n\nI’m reporting a reproducible Responses API behavior where some reasoning-capable models can return no user-visible assistant message even though output tokens are consumed.\n\n## Symptom\n\n  * Response `status=\"incomplete\"` with `incomplete_details.reason=\"max_output_tokens\"`\n  * `output` contains only `type:\"reasoning\"` items\n  * No `type:\"message\"` item is emitted (so `output_text` is empty)\n  * `usage.output_tokens` is non-zero\n\nThis can produce a blank assistant response from the client perspective.\n\n## Environment\n\n  * Date: 2026-02-07\n  * SDK: openai-python 2.17.0\n  * Platform: macOS 26.0.1 arm64\n  * Endpoint: Responses API\n\n## Minimal Python Repro\n    \n    `from openai import OpenAI\n  * Consider lowering `reasoning.effort` (model-dependent) when operating under tight budgets.\n\n## Docs Note (This Seems Documented, But Could Be Clearer)\n\nThe reasoning guide appears to already acknowledge this class of outcome:\n\n> “This might occur before any visible output tokens are produced, meaning you could incur costs for input and reasoning tokens without receiving a visible response.”\n\nSource: https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/reasoning#controlling-costs\n\nWhat would help (especially for Responses API users) is an explicit note that in this situation the response can contain only `type:\"reasoning\"` items and emit no `type:\"message\"` item (so `output_text` is empty), plus a recommended client handling pattern.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nIf someone from OpenAI can confirm whether this is expected, or whether there’s a recommended client handling pattern, I’m happy to provide more artifacts/response IDs.\n\n_j February 7, 2026, 11:15pm 2\n\nThat is completely expected.\n\nYou set a limit for how many tokens can be generated within your budget.\n\nIf the AI model exceeds that, even if it was still generating internal thinking, it gets cut off - no delivery.\n\nOn the Reponses API this is a budget for the entire turn of the input, including multiple generations that the AI may make calling tools and deliberating more using its agentic iterator for hosted tools.\n\nSet the `max_output_tokens` high.\n\nIf you want the AI to be encouraged to write less at your expense, use either `reasoning.effort` or `text.verbosity` levels - the AI knows about those.\n\nWhat IS not working right and is stealing content you paid for: non-stream Chat Completions with max_completion_tokens hit will NOT DELIVER the output that the AI model was generating into the FINAL channel.\n\nTheodorNEngoy February 7, 2026, 11:21pm 3\n\nThanks, agreed that hitting max_output_tokens explains status=“incomplete” in general.\n\nThe specific behavior I’m flagging is: the response can be entirely blank from the client POV: output contains only type:“reasoning” items, no type:“message”, so output_text is empty while usage.output_tokens > 0 and incomplete_details.reason=“max_output_tokens”.\n\nAlso, in my repro there are no tool calls (single prompt), and the blank rate tracks reasoning.effort under tight budgets (e.g. high → 100% blanks in small samples, even at higher budgets for a very short prompt).\n\nIf this is intended, it would be great to have docs explicitly call out “missing message / blank output_text” as an expected outcome and recommend the client pattern: detect missing message + reason==“max_output_tokens” and retry with a higher budget and/or lower reasoning.effort. Do you know an official doc section that confirms this behavior?\n\n_j February 7, 2026, 11:38pm 4\n\nImage TheodorNEngoy:\n\n> If this is intended, it would be great to have docs\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/reasoning#controlling-costs\n\n> …This might occur before any visible output tokens are produced, meaning you could incur costs for input and reasoning tokens without receiving a visible response.\n\nTheodorNEngoy February 7, 2026, 11:51pm 5\n\nThanks - this link is exactly what I was looking for.\n\nAgree this is consistent with the reasoning guide (costs can be incurred without a visible response when the budget is exhausted):\n\nhttps://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/reasoning#controlling-costs\n\nWhat I think would still help (esp. for Responses API users) is making it very explicit in the docs that, in this scenario, the response can contain only `type:\"reasoning\"` items and emit no `type:\"message\"` item (so `output_text` is empty), plus a recommended client handling pattern.\n\nAlso, in my trials, the blank-output rate tracks `reasoning.effort` under tight budgets (higher effort => more blanks; `high` became 100% blanks in small samples). That might be worth a one-line callout as a mitigation: lower `reasoning.effort` or retry with higher `max_output_tokens` when `reason==\"max_output_tokens\"` and no `message` output is present.\n\n_j February 7, 2026, 11:55pm 6\n\nThe different behavior of non-output tokens also being counted in the budget you set is why the parameter “max_tokens” on Chat Completions is not accepted on reasoning models, and one must then use “max_completion_tokens”.\n\n_j February 8, 2026, 12:08am 8\n\nYou can’t force everybody to read everything they might want to know before they start making API calls and setting parameters that are not required…\n\nIf you want more answers, your response object has more answers for you:\n\nimage390×190 3.74 KB\n\nTheodorNEngoy February 8, 2026, 12:20am 9\n\nGood point - the Responses API payload does contain the info (e.g. `status`, `incomplete_details`, and the `output` item types), and that’s exactly what I’m using to detect + handle the condition client-side.\n\nThe gap is mostly ergonomics/docs: from the “happy path” many clients look only at `output_text` (or stream visible text). In this failure mode you can get an empty `output_text` while still being charged, unless you inspect `output` and notice there’s no `type:\"message\"` item.\n\nSo my request is mainly that the docs make the Responses-API manifestation explicit and recommend a standard handling pattern, e.g.:\n\n  * if `status==\"incomplete\"` and `incomplete_details.reason==\"max_output_tokens\"` and no `message` output is present:\n    * treat as retryable\n    * retry with higher `max_output_tokens` (bounded retries)\n    * optionally lower `reasoning.effort` under tight budgets\n\nAlso, in my repro there are no tools/agent loop (single prompt), and the blank rate tracks `reasoning.effort` under tight budgets (higher effort => more blanks).--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFeature Request: Daily Topic Updates on ChatGPT Home Screen - Feature requests - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/feature-request-daily-topic-updates-on-chatgpt-home-screen/1373605)\nciteturn31560search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; z2sb7i9w February 7, 2026, 9:47pm 1\n\n# Feature Request: Daily Topic Updates on ChatGPT Home Screen\n\nChatGPT Feature requests\n\nz2sb7i9w February 7, 2026, 9:47pm 1\n\nI have an idea that could revolutionize the way people get knowledge. The idea is a daily topic update feed right on the ChatGPT main screen.\n\nHow it would work:\n\n  * People tell ChatGPT what topics interest them\n  * ChatGPT would automatically search for updates on those topics daily\n  * The updates would be displayed directly on the home screen\n\nBenefits:\n\n  * Saves massive time: People never again need to search for information on any topic\n  * Searching replaced: It would be far more efficient than current ways of searching or browsing.\n  * No knowledge of topic required: The feed will deliver updates even if the topic is new to you.\n  * Removes effort: People stay informed without effort.\n\nThis is incredible because, it’s not that web searching would disappear. It’s that web searching would become unnecessary.\n\nThis would dramatically reduce people’s need to use search engines, which is huge. For common, daily needs, this could make search engines almost obsolete. They’d still exist for exploration, but people’s automatic go-to for information would move to ChatGPT.\n\nz2sb7i9w February 8, 2026, 4:04am 2\n\nHere’s why this is genuinely astonishing:\n\nFor decades, the thought has been: if you want information, you must search for it. But suddenly this new idea says: Tell ChatGPT what you want to know — and it’ll keep you informed.\n\nInstead of:\n\n  * Remembering to search\n  * Knowing what to type\n  * Knowing when to search again\n\nYou just express interest once.\n\nThat’s incredible.\n\nIn short, the idea of telling ChatGPT everything you want to know about and getting updates daily, never touching search again, is mind-bending because it:\n\n  * Changes current behavior\n  * Removes present difficulty\n  * Gives latest knowledge automatically\n  * Is much more efficient\n  * Gives people free time\n\nFor most people, most of the time, it very likely would replace searching. People would abandon searching because they no longer need to. No typing queries. No opening browsers. Just say your interest once, and updates flow to you.\n\nSince ChatGPT understands what people tell it, topics can be ultra-specific. You could stay informed daily on where exactly lions live in Africa, what new clothing stores are opening in your city soon, what day a new video game will release, and other highly-specific interests.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCodex for Mac keeps crashing - latest version installed - Codex - OpenAI Developer Community (https://community.openai.com/t/codex-for-mac-keeps-crashing-latest-version-installed/1373604)\nciteturn31560search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Crawled: 8 months ago; larnaux February 7, 2026, 8:56pm 1\n\n# Codex for Mac keeps crashing - latest version installed\n\nCodex\n\nlarnaux February 7, 2026, 8:56pm 1\n\nAlso, the selector does not work\n\nDo you want me to run the backend automated test suite inside the API container to validate current behavior?\n\ndocker compo